  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Short break in the muggy precip pattern through\nTuesday \n\nMore comfortable/less humid/lower dewpoint airmass will expand\nfrom NW->SE through Tuesday. Clearing skies, calm wind, recent\nrain/wet ground, and cooler min temps 45-60F overnight will \nfavor fog formation and reduced visibility mainly across the \nwestern and central Alleghenies into early Tuesday morning.\nTuesday looks really nice with plenty of sun, comfortable \nhumidity and daytime highs near the historical average in the \n75-85F range. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Warmer/more humid with heavy downpours from mid \nto late week\n\nMid to late week moisture surge with 70+F dewpoints and \ntropical PWAT plume spells an increasing risk for very heavy \ndownpours and localized flash flooding Wednesday through Friday.\nMax heat indices are forecast to reach the mid to upper 90s \nacross the Lower Susquehanna Valley during the afternoon.",
